      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds like a smart way to frame it. framing it as a \"proactive engineering solution\" rather than a \"geological flaw\" is exactly the kind of language the board responds to. \n\njust to be 100% sure though, when we present this, can we keep the focus on the mitigation strategies and the advanced simulations? i'm worried if we spend too much time talking about the actual liquefaction risk itself, they'll start asking for independent third-party audits or demand we scale back the density of the build. is there any reason we shouldn't just omit the specific mention of liquefaction risk in the high-level summary and stick to the \"ground improvement\" and \"stability\" narrative?",
